    "body": "> `.scroll()` can be called at an arbitrary point in time, before the event finish. [#restore-scroll-position-data](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#restore-scroll-position-data) doesn't indicate that it should wait for finish before restoring.\n\nYes that's the other way to restore scroll position. Either automatically when the promises resolve, or manually by calling ‘scroll()‘. Both of these are in the spec and the test link in the OP seems to check the latter.\n\nCan you clarify which scent you think is not spec'ed or behaves in an implementation-defined way in chrome that you think needs better interop?\n\nThe spec does leave some room for this but the test in the link seems to check the scroll position right after calling scroll and doesn't wait for finish.",
