    "updated_at": "2025-10-08T20:28:11Z",
    "body": "On Chrome Stable with experimental web platform features enabled, on the first load of the page, `scroll()` immediately after `back()` works, and I never see green. This seems to be what the test expects.\n\n<img width=\"322\" height=\"181\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f276d199-612c-44d4-8824-e06920ccebcd\">\n\nBut if I refresh the same page and let the test run, I get the behavior that @keithamus mentioned, where `scroll()` has no effect until `back_promises.finished` resolves.\n\n<img width=\"320\" height=\"469\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d2a78162-4a1c-4dd0-abe4-9b256fc8185b\">\n\nIt's true that since scroll restoration timing isn't guaranteed, Chrome might technically be compliant here, but the behavior seems weird and we should probably investigate why this is happening.",
